WEBVTT

00:00:00.980 --> 00:00:03.850
<b>Doctor's Office</b>

00:00:02.110 --> 00:00:03.850
Huh? Where's Hinomaru?

00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:08.480
Oh, the doctor called him and Coach
into the office in the back.

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:10.780
It's pretty amazing...

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:14.690
We won.

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:16.690
We beat Hakuro.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:21.420
Dachi High beat Hakuro,
the strongest club in high school sumo!

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:27.300
The way you started was awesome, Hotaru!

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:30.010
It got me seriously pumped!

00:00:30.010 --> 00:00:32.460
Oh, no... I still lost my bout.

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:36.750
And what about you, Kunisaki-san?
You took down your second national treasure!

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:38.220
I know, right?

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:40.580
I'm on fire right now.

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:44.690
What if they choose me to go to All-Japan?

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:47.290
I'm so good, it's scary!

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:51.550
Whoops, another nosebleed.

00:00:53.170 --> 00:00:54.000
Here.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.450
Oh, thanks, Tsuruko.

00:00:56.450 --> 00:00:57.610
My name is Chizuko.

00:00:57.610 --> 00:01:00.310
How are you guys still so lively?

00:01:00.310 --> 00:01:03.390
I put every ounce of energy I had
into my bout, so I'm exhausted.

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:08.280
You sure had a lot of pressure on
your shoulders, huh, Yuma-san?

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:10.720
Don't act like you weren't
partly to blame for that.

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:15.130
When you lost your bout, I thought 
my heart was gonna burst.

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:17.590
Sorry about that.

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:25.460
<i>I </i>should<i> be as happy as
the rest of the team...</i>

00:01:25.820 --> 00:01:29.820
<i>So why... do I feel so uneasy?</i>

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:34.460
But yeah. Since we've made it to the final,
we've accomplished our biggest goal:

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:39.980
giving Hinomaru the chance
to face Kuze in the ring.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:45.780
Even if we lose as a team,
as long as he can win the fifth bout,

00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:48.070
his dream of going pro could come true.

00:01:48.070 --> 00:01:48.740
Yeah.

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:52.250
Hell, even if we lose,
we've still come second.

00:01:52.610 --> 00:01:54.160
Second at a national tournament.

00:01:54.160 --> 00:01:56.380
Not bad, considering where we started from.

00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:58.100
Hey now, Gojo...

00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:00.480
We've already beaten the strongest team!

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:03.300
Eiga High's gonna be no match for us.

00:02:04.030 --> 00:02:04.850
Reina-san?

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:08.730
<i>I now know... what's making me feel uneasy.</i>

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:12.110
<i>Their slack attitude!</i>

00:02:12.550 --> 00:02:14.110
Ow!

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:19.280
You're not done fighting yet!

00:02:19.650 --> 00:02:23.870
He... Hinomaru has a lot 
of battles left to fight!

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:26.980
Saying losing doesn't matter,
or that you'll win easily...

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:29.790
You can't just sit back and relax!

00:02:30.320 --> 00:02:32.790
Hinomaru was able to beat Tennoji

00:02:32.790 --> 00:02:35.550
because he saw how hard all of you fought!

00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:37.900
That's how he is, right?

00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:43.010
Kuze is even stronger than Tennoji.

00:02:43.290 --> 00:02:46.250
I'm not sure Hinomaru can even beat him.

00:02:46.710 --> 00:02:51.520
But that's all the more reason why
you have to try your hardest to win!

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:57.750
Uh... I mean...

00:02:58.190 --> 00:02:59.780
<i>Oops, I've done it now.</i>

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:05.310
Obviously, I'm not the one in the ring,
so it's not my place to say these things...

00:03:05.310 --> 00:03:07.610
Sorry for raining on your parade.

00:03:07.610 --> 00:03:08.520
No...

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:11.710
You're absolutely right, Reina-san.

00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:14.960
Thanks for telling them
what I should have been saying.

00:03:16.450 --> 00:03:18.670
It probably slipped our minds that,

00:03:18.670 --> 00:03:22.840
because Ushio lost in the individual 
tournament, even if he beats Kuze,

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:26.470
he still may not get an invite to
the All-Japan National Championships.

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:30.600
We need to do what we can to increase 
his chances, even if only by a tiny amount.

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:33.730
We'll make Dachi High
the top team in Japan,

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:38.050
and make Ushio the top wrestler
in the top school in Japan!

00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:41.240
And it won't just be for his sake.

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:44.740
I want our team to be the very best.

00:03:45.250 --> 00:03:48.620
Win or lose, this is our last match!

00:03:50.070 --> 00:03:53.290
Guys, let's win this and
smile all the way home!

00:03:53.490 --> 00:03:54.540
Yeah!

00:03:55.350 --> 00:03:56.170
Yeah!

00:03:56.350 --> 00:03:58.720
D-Did you hear all that?

00:04:00.450 --> 00:04:03.590
<i>This is the last time
this team will fight together.</i>

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:06.970
<i>I think, together, we've got what it takes.</i>

00:04:08.190 --> 00:04:09.420
<i>We'll be the best in Japan!</i>

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:43.980
<b>Team Tournament</b>

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:43.980
<b>Semi Finals</b>

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:46.990
<b>Ryugeji
High
School
(Fukuoka)</b>

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:46.990
<b>Eiga
University
High
School
(Saitama)</b>

00:05:45.050 --> 00:05:46.050
Face each other!

00:05:47.490 --> 00:05:51.950
<b>Bout 21 
"Idiot and Idiot"</b>

00:05:47.900 --> 00:05:48.990
Spirit!

00:05:53.480 --> 00:05:55.140
Railroad tracks.

00:05:55.140 --> 00:05:57.620
This is the semifinals, right?

00:06:02.680 --> 00:06:04.910
The second bout was also a walkover.

00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:08.440
The third bout, too.

00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:11.050
And the fourth.

00:06:11.790 --> 00:06:13.740
Four straight railroad track wins?

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:16.130
They're all... really huge.

00:06:32.410 --> 00:06:33.640
Spirit!

00:06:37.060 --> 00:06:38.170
The bout is over!

00:06:39.450 --> 00:06:42.630
He got scared and stepped out of the ring.

00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:44.460
The stare-out.

00:06:44.860 --> 00:06:48.510
They used to fight like that centuries ago.

00:06:48.860 --> 00:06:51.760
They're so outmatched,
you can only pity them.

00:06:51.990 --> 00:06:56.410
That guy has gone far beyond
the level of high school sumo.

00:07:00.510 --> 00:07:03.230
Ah! Hey there, Odachi.

00:07:04.440 --> 00:07:05.940
<b>Eiga
University
High School
Sumo Club</b>

00:07:05.470 --> 00:07:09.700
<i>We were no match for them
when we trained together before.</i>

00:07:10.490 --> 00:07:13.820
<i>I had no idea we'd be fighting them in
the final of a national championship.</i>

00:07:15.460 --> 00:07:19.080
<i>Facing them like this has reminded me
just how big they are.</i>

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:22.360
Long time no see, Chihiro!

00:07:22.360 --> 00:07:25.140
Sorry I missed you that time
you had make-up classes.

00:07:25.140 --> 00:07:28.890
Who woulda thought you'd take up sumo, too?

00:07:30.440 --> 00:07:32.190
Come on, dude, lighten up!

00:07:32.190 --> 00:07:34.170
We're on good terms, you and me, right?

00:07:34.170 --> 00:07:37.980
You took up sumo because 
you look up to me, didn't ya?

00:07:37.980 --> 00:07:41.100
No, I did not! Get your hands off me!
And don't talk to me!

00:07:41.650 --> 00:07:46.110
I will hate you until the day I die.

00:07:46.580 --> 00:07:48.820
<i>They seem to know each other.</i>

00:07:48.820 --> 00:07:50.690
<i>Are they friends?</i>

00:07:50.690 --> 00:07:52.490
Come now, everyone.

00:07:53.760 --> 00:07:55.590
No need to fight.

00:07:55.590 --> 00:07:59.030
Sumo is a more beautiful endeavor.

00:07:59.030 --> 00:08:00.500
Not a fight.

00:08:00.500 --> 00:08:02.400
Right, Leon-chan?

00:08:02.400 --> 00:08:04.390
Huh? What're you talking about?

00:08:04.390 --> 00:08:06.340
Sumo's nothing <i>but</i> fighting.

00:08:06.340 --> 00:08:08.990
And I'll punch you if
you call me Leon-chan again.

00:08:09.690 --> 00:08:13.180
Knock it off, you guys. This isn't the time.

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:15.250
Hang on a minute, Odachi...

00:08:15.250 --> 00:08:17.220
You're missing someone, aren't you?

00:08:17.220 --> 00:08:18.820
Will he make the final?

00:08:18.820 --> 00:08:21.100
That weed by the name of Mitsuhashi.

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:23.240
I guess he won't be there.

00:08:23.240 --> 00:08:26.440
He's a twig who got injured
because he doesn't know his limits.

00:08:26.680 --> 00:08:32.320
That's the long and short of it.
Sumo wrestlers have to be big and heavy.

00:08:32.780 --> 00:08:36.840
We'll teach you that lesson
when we contest the final.

00:08:37.220 --> 00:08:38.410
Wait a minute.

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:44.470
Do you really believe that? After all,
you've seen what our number five can do.

00:08:46.480 --> 00:08:51.210
We know that size and weight
isn't the be all and end all in sumo.

00:08:51.490 --> 00:08:52.750
It's about spirit!

00:08:55.010 --> 00:09:00.380
Save that line for when
you've beaten our number five.

00:09:07.310 --> 00:09:08.980
We don't hold back.

00:09:09.860 --> 00:09:11.260
To the death, then.

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:15.980
His victory in the individual tournament
yesterday was hard-fought.

00:09:15.980 --> 00:09:17.240
Indeed.

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:20.330
<b>Kano Akihira
(Tottori)</b>

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:20.330
<b>Kuze Sosuke
(Saitama)</b>

00:09:25.100 --> 00:09:29.340
This year's high school yokozuna
is the Kusanagi Sword,

00:09:29.340 --> 00:09:31.920
the son of famed yokozuna, Yamatokuni.

00:09:32.090 --> 00:09:35.890
He may be ready to step up to the pro league.

00:09:35.890 --> 00:09:42.310
Which would mean this is Hinomaru's last
chance to face him in high school sumo.

00:09:42.310 --> 00:09:44.770
<b>Individual Tournament
Champion</b>

00:09:42.310 --> 00:09:46.060
<b>Kuze
Sosuke</b>

00:09:42.310 --> 00:09:46.060
<b>(Saitama)</b>

00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:45.170
The individual tournament is over.

00:09:46.460 --> 00:09:50.310
But the strongest sumo wrestler
has not yet been determined.

00:09:51.330 --> 00:09:54.570
We'll find that out in
the team tournament final...

00:09:55.410 --> 00:09:57.710
In the fifth bout.

00:09:58.620 --> 00:10:01.060
<i>Isn't that right, Hinomaru?</i>

00:10:02.740 --> 00:10:04.950
Ushio, let's get going.

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:05.760
Yeah!

00:10:06.700 --> 00:10:08.400
Good luck, guys!

00:10:08.400 --> 00:10:09.200
Yeah!

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:10.290
We've got this!

00:10:18.020 --> 00:10:20.750
Have fun out there, Hinomaru.

00:10:24.550 --> 00:10:26.020
O-Oh, I mean...

00:10:26.270 --> 00:10:27.970
That's the wrong thing to say, isn't it?

00:10:27.970 --> 00:10:30.390
G-Good luck, Shorty!

00:10:32.610 --> 00:10:34.690
<i>"Have fun," huh?</i>

00:10:36.510 --> 00:10:37.280
Right!

00:10:39.870 --> 00:10:41.510
<i>The team tournament final.</i>

00:10:41.510 --> 00:10:43.870
<i>On the east side, Odachi High School.</i>

00:10:50.910 --> 00:10:53.710
<i>On the west side,
Eiga University High School.</i>

00:10:57.770 --> 00:11:00.780
Dachi High made it to the final.

00:11:00.780 --> 00:11:04.630
Yeah, but Eiga High's in the better position.

00:11:04.630 --> 00:11:05.810
You're right.

00:11:06.270 --> 00:11:10.480
Eiga sailed through their semifinal
without so much as a scratch,

00:11:10.480 --> 00:11:13.010
whereas Dachi High got
beat up against Hakuro.

00:11:13.860 --> 00:11:16.400
They've revealed all of 
their trump cards, too.

00:11:16.950 --> 00:11:19.620
This will come down to
who has the most spirit.

00:11:19.620 --> 00:11:23.700
That's why they'll try to hit the ground
running by leading off with...

00:11:25.800 --> 00:11:27.870
We're counting on you, Kunisaki!

00:11:28.320 --> 00:11:30.520
<i>On the east side, Kunisaki-kun.</i>

00:11:33.670 --> 00:11:36.630
You're a real crowd-pleaser, Chihiro!

00:11:36.900 --> 00:11:38.940
<i>On the west side, Hyodo-kun.</i>

00:11:40.410 --> 00:11:44.760
Well, beating two national treasures
was bound to get the crowd on your side.

00:11:45.050 --> 00:11:48.590
And so soon after taking up sumo.
Color me impressed.

00:11:49.760 --> 00:11:50.770
But...

00:11:51.860 --> 00:11:57.240
You're not going to outshine 
your big brother, Chihiro!

00:11:59.050 --> 00:12:01.920
Hyodo is your brother?!

00:12:01.920 --> 00:12:04.910
Our parents divorced when I was five,

00:12:05.150 --> 00:12:07.930
and he went to live with our father.

00:12:07.930 --> 00:12:12.540
I hated the guy, so I stayed with our mother.

00:12:13.190 --> 00:12:14.600
That jerk...

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:22.050
All I remember about him
is how oppressive he was!

00:12:22.540 --> 00:12:23.890
I'll be the one...

00:12:23.890 --> 00:12:26.340
who takes on Hyodo Masato.

00:12:26.900 --> 00:12:29.120
It has to be me!

00:12:30.050 --> 00:12:31.250
Hands on the ground.

00:12:32.360 --> 00:12:34.250
Just like his brother,

00:12:34.250 --> 00:12:37.920
Hyodo's latent sumo talents are on par
with a national treasure's.

00:12:38.980 --> 00:12:41.420
But only on par with.

00:12:41.820 --> 00:12:44.740
There's a reason Hyodo doesn't
have a national treasure moniker.

00:12:45.350 --> 00:12:50.290
Hey, Chihiro, I like that Mitsuhashi kid.

00:12:50.560 --> 00:12:54.370
That move he pulled in your
semifinal sent chills up my spine!

00:12:55.620 --> 00:12:58.100
A reason he doesn't have
a national treasure moniker?

00:12:58.100 --> 00:13:00.340
Yeah. It's because...

00:13:02.030 --> 00:13:03.230
Spirit!

00:13:07.570 --> 00:13:08.640
Hey!

00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:15.110
...he's an idiot.

00:13:19.340 --> 00:13:20.640
<i>What d'ya think, Chihiro?</i>

00:13:20.640 --> 00:13:22.320
<i>I bet you're surprised.</i>

00:13:22.890 --> 00:13:27.410
<i>When you lose it and charge at me,
I'll leap out of the way—</i>

00:13:27.850 --> 00:13:29.720
You skipped too many steps!

00:13:29.720 --> 00:13:31.870
Hyodo-san, you colossal idiot!

00:13:31.870 --> 00:13:33.330
W-Wait, Chihiro!

00:13:33.970 --> 00:13:38.450
Hyodo is sometimes so tricky, 
he digs his own grave.

00:13:38.450 --> 00:13:39.080
But...

00:13:39.290 --> 00:13:40.290
Hey!

00:13:40.830 --> 00:13:42.250
I said wait!

00:13:42.750 --> 00:13:47.050
His tricky techniques and athletic ability
allow him to take down huge opponents!

00:13:47.840 --> 00:13:52.180
You need to listen to your 
older brother, Chihiro!

00:13:52.740 --> 00:13:55.930
The only one who can fight
an idiot like him...

00:13:56.690 --> 00:13:58.310
<i>Leap!</i>

00:13:57.940 --> 00:13:58.070
<b>Leap</b>

00:13:58.070 --> 00:13:58.440
<b>Leap</b>

00:13:58.440 --> 00:13:58.940
<b>Leap</b>

00:13:59.280 --> 00:14:01.360
...is another idiot!

00:14:02.830 --> 00:14:04.490
What the hell kinda bout is this?

00:14:05.130 --> 00:14:08.410
<i>He always takes what's dear to me...</i>

00:14:10.980 --> 00:14:12.720
What'cha got there, Chihiro?

00:14:12.720 --> 00:14:14.660
That looks like fun.

00:14:16.610 --> 00:14:18.830
Oh, is it over already?

00:14:20.830 --> 00:14:23.360
<i>...messes everything up, and waltzes off!</i>

00:14:24.880 --> 00:14:29.300
<i>But not this time! Dachi High dream
to be Japan's best is important to me,</i>

00:14:29.730 --> 00:14:31.220
<i>and you won't take that away from me!</i>

00:14:33.010 --> 00:14:34.770
Okay, I'll jump, too!

00:14:35.440 --> 00:14:37.200
<i>What the heck is he doing?</i>

00:14:37.200 --> 00:14:39.190
<i>So he won't let me to grab his belt, huh?</i>

00:14:39.570 --> 00:14:41.150
<i>In that case...</i>

00:14:41.150 --> 00:14:43.470
<i>Flash Attack!</i>

00:14:43.150 --> 00:14:43.280
<b>Flash Attack</b>

00:14:43.280 --> 00:14:43.650
<b>Flash Attack</b>

00:14:43.650 --> 00:14:43.900
<b>Flash Attack</b>

00:14:43.900 --> 00:14:46.070
<i>How do you like that?!</i>

00:14:46.400 --> 00:14:48.270
Hyodo Masato?!

00:14:49.220 --> 00:14:51.200
What about him, Kunisaki-san?

00:14:52.110 --> 00:14:54.450
Nothing. Please continue.

00:14:54.840 --> 00:14:57.840
Hyodo has only been doing 
sumo for two years,

00:14:57.840 --> 00:15:00.720
but he's earned a spot as a regular
on the powerful Eiga High team.

00:15:01.810 --> 00:15:03.360
This is from the spring tournament.

00:15:03.360 --> 00:15:07.010
As you can see, he's very unpredictable.

00:15:07.320 --> 00:15:11.510
His power, speed, and killer
instinct are all first class.

00:15:12.030 --> 00:15:14.000
<i>So it's your second year, huh?</i>

00:15:14.000 --> 00:15:15.970
<i>It's only my first!</i>

00:15:17.690 --> 00:15:22.730
<i>You'd always take up whatever
I was doing, outdo me, then quit.</i>

00:15:23.500 --> 00:15:25.650
<i>But this time, it's the other way around!</i>

00:15:26.000 --> 00:15:29.900
<i>It's only my first year,
and I've already beaten national treasures!</i>

00:15:30.270 --> 00:15:31.910
<i>This is incredible!</i>

00:15:32.760 --> 00:15:33.280
I can't see!

00:15:34.190 --> 00:15:35.300
There!

00:15:36.090 --> 00:15:37.020
A minor inner foot sweep!

00:15:37.020 --> 00:15:40.370
Hey, you're using my techniques.

00:15:40.540 --> 00:15:43.300
You'd better do them justice, Kunisaki!

00:15:43.630 --> 00:15:46.130
<i>You damn monkey!</i>

00:15:46.320 --> 00:15:48.760
A leg grab won't work!

00:15:49.130 --> 00:15:49.720
You...

00:15:49.950 --> 00:15:51.090
Gotcha!

00:15:52.840 --> 00:15:54.800
Put your hand down!

00:15:54.930 --> 00:15:57.890
Are you just screwing around?!

00:15:58.190 --> 00:16:00.730
You're getting erratic...

00:16:00.900 --> 00:16:02.370
Chihiro!

00:16:04.100 --> 00:16:05.290
<i>An overarm throw?!</i>

00:16:05.690 --> 00:16:07.720
Ow, hey!

00:16:08.860 --> 00:16:10.070
You won't get away!

00:16:11.820 --> 00:16:13.160
A test of strength?!

00:16:13.300 --> 00:16:15.680
That doesn't really look like sumo.

00:16:15.680 --> 00:16:16.990
They're both incredible!

00:16:17.320 --> 00:16:19.370
<i>You need to calm down, Kunisaki-san!</i>

00:16:19.770 --> 00:16:22.960
<i>You can beat him if you just focus!</i>

00:16:23.240 --> 00:16:25.830
That was cheating!

00:16:27.470 --> 00:16:29.550
The idea popped into my head,
so I just had to do it!

00:16:29.550 --> 00:16:32.110
Damn it. Fight seriously—

00:16:32.590 --> 00:16:33.880
<i>He's...</i>

00:16:35.080 --> 00:16:37.300
This Hyodo guy...

00:16:38.210 --> 00:16:40.500
He really enjoys sumo wrestling.

00:16:41.430 --> 00:16:44.090
<i>With all his fooling around,
it's hard to notice,</i>

00:16:44.460 --> 00:16:45.850
<i>but up close, I can tell.</i>

00:16:46.540 --> 00:16:49.450
<i>The brother who always used to
get bored of stuff and walk away</i>

00:16:49.450 --> 00:16:51.650
<i>has spent time building up...</i>

00:16:52.080 --> 00:16:53.700
<i>a sumo wrestler's body!</i>

00:16:55.650 --> 00:16:59.120
<i>Watching Hyodo fight is 
really bad for my heart.</i>

00:16:59.460 --> 00:17:03.870
<i>He can beat someone better than him,
then turn around and lose to someone worse.</i>

00:17:04.390 --> 00:17:08.890
<i>He makes it hard to predict how many bouts
you're going to win in a team match.</i>

00:17:09.330 --> 00:17:13.260
<i>But he only took up
sumo wrestling two years ago.</i>

00:17:13.340 --> 00:17:17.970
<b>Eiga
University
High School
Sumo Club</b>

00:17:13.730 --> 00:17:17.650
<i>Back then, he'd join a club, cause a fuss,
get kicked out, and repeat.</i>

00:17:17.650 --> 00:17:20.020
<i>Until he eventually made it to the sumo club,</i>

00:17:20.760 --> 00:17:24.360
<i>challenged us to a fight, 
and was knocked flat on his back.</i>

00:17:27.140 --> 00:17:30.350
So this is sumo, an openweight sport, huh?

00:17:31.550 --> 00:17:33.500
<i>He's an idiot, for sure.</i>

00:17:34.080 --> 00:17:34.900
<i>But...</i>

00:17:35.550 --> 00:17:37.190
<i>He loves sumo.</i>

00:17:37.510 --> 00:17:43.910
<i>His pure joy for the sport makes you
want to just let him do his thing.</i>

00:17:45.170 --> 00:17:48.180
Chihiro, do you love sumo?

00:17:49.110 --> 00:17:51.140
I know I do!

00:17:51.140 --> 00:17:55.920
I finally found something 
I can be proud of myself for!

00:17:56.170 --> 00:17:58.010
What about you?

00:17:58.010 --> 00:18:00.870
Why are you doing sumo?

00:18:02.550 --> 00:18:04.420
<i>After I lost to Hinomaru,</i>

00:18:04.880 --> 00:18:08.020
<i>I got interested in sumo,
the art he used to beat me.</i>

00:18:08.540 --> 00:18:12.450
<i>But maybe it's like wrestling...</i>

00:18:09.270 --> 00:18:10.020
<b>Chihiro
 Special #13</b>

00:18:10.020 --> 00:18:10.400
<b>Chihiro
 Special #13</b>

00:18:10.400 --> 00:18:10.940
<b>Chihiro
 Special #13</b>

00:18:12.450 --> 00:18:17.830
<i>Just one step on the path to becoming 
the top mixed martial artist.</i>

00:18:18.870 --> 00:18:24.050
<i>So, compared to Hinomaru and
the other national treasures...</i>

00:18:25.850 --> 00:18:29.710
Chihiro, you don't need to 
compare yourself to anyone.

00:18:30.010 --> 00:18:31.400
Your feelings are still real.

00:18:34.660 --> 00:18:35.760
Bring it!

00:18:36.130 --> 00:18:38.760
<i>That's right. That goes for me, too.</i>

00:18:39.050 --> 00:18:43.100
<i>Kunisaki-san's putting his
head down and charging!</i>

00:18:44.750 --> 00:18:47.020
<i>I love sumo!</i>

00:18:47.640 --> 00:18:51.090
<i>He doesn't have the sharp footwork
nor shift techniques that Hinomaru does.</i>

00:18:51.090 --> 00:18:53.130
<i>His headbutts are...</i>

00:18:55.580 --> 00:18:58.890
<i>I've never worked on my headbutting.</i>

00:18:59.220 --> 00:19:01.750
<i>I sidelined it to focus on winning!</i>

00:19:02.250 --> 00:19:05.160
<i>But I had to try it just now!</i>

00:19:05.550 --> 00:19:09.710
<i>As a sumo wrestler,
I didn't want to run away from sumo!</i>

00:19:11.470 --> 00:19:13.540
<i>Sorry... guys...</i>

00:19:15.200 --> 00:19:17.380
You want to be the strongest, don't you?!

00:19:17.800 --> 00:19:19.000
Kunisaki-san!

00:19:20.020 --> 00:19:21.260
The strongest in guile!

00:19:21.560 --> 00:19:22.970
And the strongest in sumo!

00:19:23.440 --> 00:19:24.720
Don't lose!

00:19:24.860 --> 00:19:28.730
Supreme! Invincible! The strongest!

00:19:29.300 --> 00:19:31.830
<i>Clasped hand twist drop throw!</i>

00:19:31.830 --> 00:19:34.870
<i>Neo Chihiro Special #2!</i>

00:19:31.980 --> 00:19:32.110
<b>Clasped hand twist drop throw
Neo Chihiro Special #2</b>

00:19:32.110 --> 00:19:32.480
<b>Clasped hand twist drop throw
Neo Chihiro Special #2</b>

00:19:32.480 --> 00:19:35.610
<b>Clasped hand twist drop throw
Neo Chihiro Special #2</b>

00:19:35.820 --> 00:19:37.900
I figured you'd try that!

00:19:38.880 --> 00:19:40.240
<i>Sorry, Chihiro!</i>

00:19:40.770 --> 00:19:46.000
<i>You're not the only one who knows both
wrestling techniques and sumo ones!</i>

00:19:46.600 --> 00:19:48.200
West side wins!

00:19:51.490 --> 00:19:55.020
That headbutt put him 
at a serious disadvantage.

00:19:55.020 --> 00:19:58.530
Yeah, in a battle of physiques...

00:19:58.530 --> 00:20:01.340
...Dachi High can't keep up.

00:20:01.840 --> 00:20:06.850
There wasn't a big difference in their
physiques in this first bout, though.

00:20:06.850 --> 00:20:11.810
I'm more impressed by how 
Hyodo handled that last throw.

00:20:12.200 --> 00:20:14.350
They're so similar.

00:20:14.350 --> 00:20:17.260
Maybe they each understood
what the other was about.

00:20:17.860 --> 00:20:21.030
Well, looks I win again...

00:20:21.460 --> 00:20:22.650
Chihiro.

00:20:23.990 --> 00:20:26.700
I seriously hate you.

00:20:27.000 --> 00:20:29.310
You ate my food,

00:20:29.310 --> 00:20:32.040
used my saved data to beat my games,

00:20:32.610 --> 00:20:34.880
took my allowance...

00:20:35.120 --> 00:20:37.540
But what pisses me off the most...

00:20:38.100 --> 00:20:41.050
is that you're really strong.

00:20:44.040 --> 00:20:49.640
I'm not sure what you mean, 
but that was a fun sumo bout.

00:20:50.660 --> 00:20:52.040
Maybe.

00:20:55.160 --> 00:20:58.020
That's a painful loss.

00:20:58.020 --> 00:21:00.210
It'll be a shock for the team.

00:21:00.550 --> 00:21:01.770
Yeah.

00:21:01.770 --> 00:21:03.530
You think?

00:21:04.310 --> 00:21:07.010
You could have won that bout, Kunisaki-san.

00:21:07.010 --> 00:21:09.410
Yeah, my bad.

00:21:09.840 --> 00:21:11.610
I'm counting on you.

00:21:12.980 --> 00:21:18.040
<i>There are two Dachi High members
who I could never beat in practice.</i>

00:21:18.520 --> 00:21:20.400
<i>One was Hinomaru.</i>

00:21:20.400 --> 00:21:21.920
<i>And the other was...</i>

00:21:22.390 --> 00:21:24.930
I wasn't expecting to start off with a loss.

00:21:26.210 --> 00:21:28.290
I'll just have to adapt.

00:21:29.330 --> 00:21:32.610
<i>Second bout. On the east side, Tsuji-kun.</i>

00:23:06.000 --> 00:23:06.850
Yo!

00:23:07.240 --> 00:23:09.320
Dude, let's arm wrestle.

00:23:09.320 --> 00:23:11.200
I don't arm wrestle.

00:23:12.140 --> 00:23:12.980
Yo!

00:23:13.440 --> 00:23:14.950
Let's thumb wrestle.

00:23:14.950 --> 00:23:16.950
I don't thumb wrestle.

00:23:17.260 --> 00:23:19.450
So what kind of wrestling <i>do</i> you do?

00:23:26.500 --> 00:23:28.820
You're good at this...

00:23:27.460 --> 00:23:30.970
<b>Next Bout  "The Forgotten National Treasure, Onikiri Yasutsuna"</b>

00:23:28.820 --> 00:23:30.040
What the heck is this?
